1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,380
Isis fled danger with the child Horus.

2
00:00:04,320 --> 00:00:07,000
Seven scorpions guarded her as she traveled,

3
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:10,320
vulnerable despite her divine identity.

4
00:00:11,260 --> 00:00:13,380
A wealthy woman closed her door to

5
00:00:13,380 --> 00:00:16,600
them. A poorer woman welcomed the travelers,

6
00:00:17,380 --> 00:00:19,240
offering what little shelter she could.

7
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:22,080
The scorpions took revenge.

8
00:00:22,760 --> 00:00:25,500
One carried their gathered venom and stung

9
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:27,300
the wealthy woman’s child,

10
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:31,097
turning a refusal of hospitality into tragedy.

11
00:00:32,300 --> 00:00:33,960
The mother pleaded for help.

12
00:00:34,420 --> 00:00:36,700
Isis heard the grief and refused to

13
00:00:36,700 --> 00:00:38,760
let an innocent child pay for the

14
00:00:38,760 --> 00:00:39,750
adult’s action.

15
00:00:40,860 --> 00:00:43,600
Through powerful spoken names and magic,

16
00:00:44,320 --> 00:00:45,860
Isis drew out the poison.

17
00:00:46,580 --> 00:00:47,720
The child recovered,

18
00:00:47,720 --> 00:00:50,280
and the household learned what had been

19
00:00:50,280 --> 00:00:51,517
denied at its door.

20
00:00:52,900 --> 00:00:55,320
The story does not end with revenge.

21
00:00:55,320 --> 00:00:58,500
Its strongest image is a goddess saving

22
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:00,260
someone who had turned her away.
